  Also flash-snr.py's write-gate checks /devices/rtr-5e1a8d — DMIT-only device — that does protect. But the 方案's claim "目标改 DMIT" is only partially true: the ensure_tunnel fallback now points to DMIT (need to verify line 45-58), but a pre-existing stale tunnel on 18444 to DO would pass health check and be reused — then the identity pre-check in flash-snr would catch it (rtr-5e1a8d returns 404 on DO). So the gate works but flow would abort rather than auto-correct. SOP 增补三 #4 said "改为失败重试一次（脚本内嵌 MGMT_API_BASE=8444 纠正）" — but flash-snr.py I read has NO retry and no MGMT_API_BASE correction; it just sys.exit(3) on pre-check failure. Let me check: flash-snr.py lines 243-246 — pre-check fails → exit 3, no retry, no 8444 fallback. So SOP 增补（三）#4 claims a fix ("失败重试一次（脚本内嵌 MGMT_API_BASE=8444 纠正）") that is NOT in the script. Discrepancy between SOP and script! Unless it was later removed. The current script has no retry. So the SOP statement is stale/false, and the 方案 §2.1-#1's "已修" is also overstated regarding auto-correction.

  Let me read ensure_tunnel lines 42-62 fully to be precise.Now I have what I need. Key findings on mgmt_api_test:

  - ensure_tunnel: if health on BASE (default 18444) responds, it returns immediately — a stale 18444 tunnel pointing to DO would be reused silently. The V2 fix only changed the fallback target (when building a NEW tunnel) to DMIT. So "目标改 DMIT" is half-true. flash-snr's write-gate (rtr-5e1a8d) catches the stale-DO case and aborts with zero writes — good — but then the run dies at step 4, requiring manual fix (kill stale tunnel). SOP 增补（三）#4 claims "改为失败重试一次（脚本内嵌 MGMT_API_BASE=8444 纠正）" — but flash-snr.py has NO such retry (lines 243-246 exit immediately). So SOP overstates; the 方案 §2.1-#1 inherits the overstatement. Also the stale-tunnel hazard is EXACTLY the R7 case; on the flash PC, the user's own 管理台通道-DMIT.bat uses 8444, while old 雅典娜/R4 channels may hold 18444. Real risk remains for the upcoming 4-device run: if any stale 18444 tunnel exists, batch run aborts at step 4 for every device — "无人值守" breaks. 方案 does not list a pre-flight check (netstat 18444 ownership) in §四. That's a concrete gap for "不要有遗漏".

  - Concurrency: four parallel flash-snr processes each call ensure_tunnel. If tunnel absent, all four Popen ssh -f -L 18444 — first wins, others fail with ExitOnForwardFailure (exit silently in background), then health check succeeds anyway via the winner's tunnel. Mostly benign. token(): TOKEN_FILE shared — four processes may concurrently write .mgmt-token; json.dump non-atomic could produce a truncated file read by another process → token() falls back to re-login (json.load raises → except → re-login). Benign-ish. Not worth heavy flagging, but worth a line.

  Also note: health endpoint responding ≠ correct backend; the write-gate covers writes. But steps that READ (wait_final GET /api/v1/tasks, assignments POST) all go through the same gate-guarded flow after step 4, fine.

  Now another check: 方案 §2.1-#7 "REJECT-SELFHEAL 自压（R1-R4+R7 落地并经真实重载验证）" vs SOP 增补（四） "⚠️ R2-R6 同病…修复待授权逐台做". Conflict. SOP 增补（四） dated 2026-10-13; 方案 dated 2026-10-14. Unless something happened on 10-14 (增补五 mentions "R7 实机重启 18 项验证" but not R2-R6 QUIC fixes), 方案's claim contradicts the authoritative SOP. Flag as 存疑/冲突.

  Also 方案 §3.2 R2 "mihomo 推送与 agent 栈部署顺序对调（先推大文件再装小件，减少失败重推成本）" — the rationale is backwards as I analyzed. Also reordering steps has risk: mihomo step 7 currently depends on /etc/mihomo created in step 5 (mkdir -p /etc/mihomo in step 5's run block) — actually step 7 pushes to /etc/mihomo/GeoSite.dat; the mkdir is in step 5's script. If mihomo push moved before agent stack, must move mkdir too. Minor implementation coupling the 方案 doesn't mention.

  Also R2 轮询 10s→6s: trivial gain; the wait is dominated by actual task time. And "总目标单台≤4 分钟" unsupported.

  方案 §四 gaps:
  - No pre-flight checklist: PC 侧（18444/8444 隧道归属、台账可读、DMIT 可达、固件文件存在）、设备侧（同批次固件/型号 MT7981 指纹已内置✅）。
  - No restart-verification step (SOP 增补四方法论 requires real reboot validation; several R7 root causes only manifested after reboot). 方案 §五 acceptance is all pre-reboot state. For "不要有遗漏" this is the biggest hole: WiFi 开机策略、MAC 固定生效、PCDN 复活、QUIC 竞态、cron 厂商重写 — all only verifiable after reboot. 方案 should include "刷完后至少一次重启+终验复跑（或 R7 式 18 项）"。
  - 验收 §五 "PCDN 六面净（进程/端口/S 自启/钩子/弹药/分区无执行文件）" exceeds script's gate 9 (process count only). Gap between 方案's own acceptance criteria and script capability; 方案 §3.2 doesn't propose adding port/S-link/hook/ammo/partition checks to 终验.
  - R7 实机增补删除项（rathole/zcon 二进制、厂商云 cgi 端点 cgi-exec/upload/download/backup、checkMem）未回灌脚本 —— 方案 §3.2 未列。SOP 增补（五） documents these as R7 final state; new four devices won't get them. Real omission.
  - 每日 0 点重启 caution for 无人值守站点 (SOP red line; R4 33.5h 事故). 方案 §四 doesn't ask user to confirm deployment scenario. Medium.
  - 方案 §四.2 says "编号 R8-R11、端口 13230-13233" hardcoded; script computes dynamically — fine but the 方案 presents them as fixed; if anything changed, actual may differ. Minor.

  Also: 方案 §二 2.1 table's 现状 column generally accurate per my spot checks (#2, #4, #5 verified in code). #1 partially overstated (stale tunnel reuse path remains; abort not auto-correct; SOP-claimed retry absent). #3 verified: flash-batch has 型号准入+精确 MAC. ✅. #8 honest (notes no auto-resume). 

  方案 §3.2-R1 断点自恢复 risks:
  - /tmp on OpenWrt is tmpfs — flag files lost on reboot/power-cycle, exactly the interruption scenarios; resume would then mis-detect. Must use /etc/routermgmt/state/ or similar persistent path. 方案 says /tmp/flash-N.stepK — flawed as written.
  - Step 0/1 re-entry: after step 1-2, telnet disabled and password changed; re-run dies at Tel() connect or login. Auto-skip must also switch entry transport to SSH. 方案 doesn't address. SOP §五 checkpoint method is the fallback; R1 should be designed as "skip + SSH entry" not just flag files.
  - Risk of false-positive flags producing half-configured devices that pass? No — 11-gate final verification catches; acceptable backstop. But batch --auto unattended + auto-resume could mask repeated partial failures. Moderate.

  Also flash-batch: `found = found[:args.max]` — if user plugs 4 devices plus an old factory-state device, max=4 arbitrary selection (sorted by IP). Fine.

  One more: 方案 §四.2 "四线程并行" — flash-batch default --max 4 ✅.

  Coverage assessment of user requirement: 需求4条全部有对应章节，无大遗漏；偏离点 = §五 验收超出脚本能力未给出落地路径（可视为加戏/空头支票），§2.2 时长数据与 §四.3 不一致。私加戏：R2 顺序对调属于非必要改动且理由存疑（不过用户要求"根据各 ai 意见修订"，若某 ai 提过则不算私加，但方案未注明来源）。

  Security observations:
  - UNIFIED_PW hardcoded plaintext in flash-snr.py:21 (and in SOP doc). AGENTS.md says reports/输出不显示密码；the 方案 itself doesn't leak it ✅. But "标准化"未涵盖凭证管理（硬编码+git 仓库）。Worth one bullet.
  - tb_sh embeds pubkey lines in ssh command — fine.
  - flash-snr writes .snr{N}-pw without chmod 600 (line 164) — pkg json gets 0600 but pw file doesn't. Minor inconsistency.
  - requests verify=False — existing pattern.
  - 方案 §四 cron 无人值守：auto mode flashes any factory-state MT7981 device that appears on the two subnets with zero human confirmation — 防误刷 relies on MAC sets; if a friend's/factory-fresh different-ownership device is plugged in it gets flashed. That's intended. But combined with stale-tunnel abort: cron would retry every 10 min, each attempt dying at step 4 after password changed... wait — second attempt: telnet disabled? No — step 4 abort happens AFTER step 2 (telnet killed in step 2? telnetd is in the disable list step 2, and killall telnetd at line 204). So a failed run leaves device with changed password + telnet dead; next cron scan: telnet closed → sweep (port 23) won't even find it → device invisible, silently dropped from batch, "无人值守" permanently stuck with a half-flashed device that no longer shows up in scans. That's a REAL operational hole for the 4-device plan: any failure after step 2 makes the device undiscoverable by flash-batch (which discovers via telnet:23 + factory password). 方案 §四.4 "失败台按检查点续跑修复" requires MANUAL ssh — so "零其他操作" claim breaks on any mid-run failure. This is worth flagging prominently: discovery mechanism only sees virgin devices; failed devices vanish from the pipeline. Mitigation: batch should also track in-progress devices (e.g., ledger of found IPs) or 方案 should state failure handling is manual with precise commands.

  Enough findings. Also verify 方案 §2.2 "发布任务串行等待...各台独立任务互不阻塞" — consistent with per-device tasks. OK.

  Check 方案 §五 "平台心跳秒级" — heartbeat interval? agent heartbeat maybe 30s/60s; "秒级" plausible. Skip.

